WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.890
Thousands gather outside Hungary's state broadcaster
in Budapest.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:16.960
They're here because of this:
Opposition MPs being thrown out of Hungary's

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.950
state broadcaster building…

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:27.710
They had wanted to read a list of demands
on national television; demands linked to

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:36.310
a week of escalating street demonstrations.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.730
Night after night, protestors have returned
to the streets -- there were around 10,000

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.190
over the weekend.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:52.460
It is a very good TV-channel for fairy tales.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:57.170
They don't broadcast the kind of story that
I would show my children in the future.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.409
Unions and opposition groups organised demonstrations
against a new labour law, recently approved

00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:05.950
by Prime Minister Victor Orban’s large parliamentary
majority.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.700
The law - dubbed by critics as the ‘slave
law’ - allows employers to ask staff to

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:17.460
do 400 hours of overtime per year, and delay
payment for it by up to three months.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.670
Demonstrators are unhappy with the labour
law... and with the direction Hungary is going.

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:25.780
We don't want to go back to the communist
times.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:31.890
What we are experiencing now in Hungary, wasn't
seen during communism; this level of oppression

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.570
and corruption.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.039
Something must be done.

00:01:37.039 --> 00:01:38.899
This cannot go on.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:43.990
Prime Minister Victor Orban -- and his policies
-- are very popular amongst Hungarians.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:50.100
Yet, these protests show that there is a sizeable
and vocal section of Hungarian society that

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.570
opposes him.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:59.229
It's the biggest and most visible challenge
yet to what critics - at home and abroad - see

00:01:59.229 --> 00:05:18.760
as Orban's slide towards authoritarian rule.

